f3n, hoping to catch the last bus of line 39 that takes you home.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3900380/extras/e1ae2647cc5900eb8144fce7ad302f1e.avif?t=1767958768\" width=616 height=346 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >After a terrifying encounter with a sock vendor, the 39 finally appears. You try to wave it down, but it drives right past you, leaving you stranded in the neighborhood. You have to find a way back\u2014tomorrow you take the exam that will determine whether you graduate or not. Good luck.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3900380/extras/709e7049dce81b4a1f063b9c72279fd3.avif?t=1767958768\" width=616 height=346 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The aesthetic of <i>&quot;El 39&quot;</i> is inspired by classic titles like <i>Silent Hill</i> and <i>Resident Evil</i>.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3900380/extras/b66e0c407ee59ddd994b461733fff399.avif?t=1767958768\" width=616 height=346 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>This is mixed with elements of Argentine popular culture found throughout the game, full of interactables and humor, giving way to what we call a \u201cpopcorn horror.\u201d</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Graffiti</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3900380/extras/9e3075429d3592eb309d1851a700e688.avif?t=1767958768\" width=616 height=346 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3900380/extras/b772aba